<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia KLIH suspension extended.</title>
<headline>Malaysia KLIH suspension extended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange has extended the suspension of trading in the shares of Kuala Lumpur Industries Holdings Bhd by 10 trading days.</p>
<p>It said the extension was being granted starting from Monday to enable KLIH make announcements on its various proposals.</p>
<p>The share was suspended on April 30. It last traded at 2.96 ringgit.</p>
<p>On Monday, KLIH also announced a net loss of 11.76 million ringgit for the year to March 31, 1997, against a profit of 17.17 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>The company said its losses were a result of a slowdown in the property market and the start up costs of MEC, its electrical products project.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
